From a4b3d9001dd0d50bce64634c35754b146846b9d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 06:59:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] WIP: keep schemars 0.8's schema shapes for generated clients

schemars 1 references newtype-variant payloads and documented transparent
types as definitions, which 0.8 inlined, and inlines AgentPath, which 0.8
defined; the Python SDK then lost ResultThreadItem, FileIdThreadItem and
AgentPath. #[schemars(inline)] and a hand-written AgentPath schema restore
the 0.8 shapes. schemars 1 also honors the untagged Other variant of
CodexErrorInfo and writes it as null, so the open-ended error schema lists
"other" and accepts any string or object again. The hooks schemas write
their event names as const on purpose, so only the two derived hooks
types whose single values 0.8 wrote as enum keep that form.
